specs/system-speckit/033-system-speckit-v4/036-goal-unification/010-repo-wide-goal-research/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-state.jsonl:6:{"type":"iteration","iteration":4,"newInfoRatio":0.80,"status":"complete","focus":"ring 4 — everything else that touches a goal","ring":"everything else that touches a goal","recordedAt":"2026-09-12T09:20:00Z","findings":11,"contradictions":4,"precisionGaps":3,"resolvedQuestions":4,"corrections":1,"artifacts":["iterations/iteration-004.md","deltas/iter-004.jsonl"],"novelty":"Ring 4 resolves all four ring-3 questions: the hub flag row is hand-maintained in three agreeing rosters; dist is in step and freshness-gated so ring 3 describes shipped behaviour; root rules restate posture only and contain zero goal mentions; the catalogues/playbooks do not describe the budget at all and carry six other defects. New findings include the three-way resume divergence, two incompatible status vocabularies, a dead constitutional citation behind CC-029 and its benchmark JSON, a stale command filename in CL-007, stale suite/test counts in CO-039 (observed 8 suites / 137 pass), a plugins-README rule that computes to the dead SYSTEM_GOAL_DISABLED, the root README's every-turn claim vs Cursor sessionStart-only, the legacy pi-<sha256>.json filename expectation in PI-021, the four-way goal vocabulary collision, and CE-P03's misplaced injection-only reason. R1-F1 is downgraded to local drift plus the misleading rule statement.","openQuestionsForRing5":["which contradictions are defects to fix versus deliberate surface differences needing a documented mapping (flag naming, resume, status vocabularies, budget scope, injection-only wording)","which single surface should own each fact after unification: the flag pair, the budget numbers, the status vocabulary, the runtime support matrix","should the rot-prone playbook paths and counts get a machine check, and which surfaces should it cover","does the public README budget sentence belong there at all given both retrieval lanes exclude it","is the goal vocabulary collision worth a naming note in the deep-review reference"]}
